Description: Parse every CSS colour and draw it at more than 8 bits
 librsvg kept only rgb(), hsl() and hwb() of what cssparser-color parses and
 rejected lab(), lch(), oklab(), oklch() and color() as "unsupported color
 syntax"; the CSS Color HDR spaces, color-mix() and relative colours did not
 parse at all.  The declaration was dropped and the shape painted black, and
 the message reached only RSVG_LOG.  Colours that did parse were stored as
 8-bit RGBA.  This adds a parser for the whole <color> grammar of CSS Color 4,
 CSS Color 5 and CSS Color HDR (css_color.rs) that keeps each colour in its
 own space in double precision; solid colours and gradient stops reach cairo
 as doubles, gamut mapped into sRGB as CSS Color 4 section 14.2 says when
 they are outside it, which is logged.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Origin: vendor, Sparky Stereo OS (ORDER 348)
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-02
